# Cloudflare Pages — URL redirects
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# Format: /from /to [status]   (301 default; 302 temporary; 200 rewrite)
#
# SPA routing is handled automatically: the build output has no top-level
# 404.html, so Cloudflare Pages treats this as a single-page app and serves
# index.html for unmatched navigation paths (deep links route client-side).
#
# Do NOT add a "/* /index.html 200" catch-all. It makes a request for a
# missing hashed JS chunk (e.g. after a deploy, when a browser holds a stale
# index.html) fall back to index.html, so the browser receives text/html for a
# module script and throws "Failed to load module script … MIME type
# text/html". Cloudflare also flags the catch-all as an infinite loop.
# Stale-chunk recovery is handled client-side (see src/index.html).
#
# Real content redirects go here as URLs evolve, e.g.:
#   /old-slug /new-slug 301
